Chapter: Zigbee

 Zigbee network (NWK) and application support (APS) layer framing, which
 ride on top of the IEEE 802.15.4 MAC. The NWK header routes a frame
 across the mesh (frame control, 16-bit destination and source, radius,
 sequence); the APS header addresses an application endpoint (frame
 control, destination endpoint, cluster and profile identifiers, source
 endpoint, counter). All multi-byte fields are little-endian. This is
 the Zigbee PRO 2007 frame format.

Section: NWK Frame Control

 The NWK frame control (two bytes): frame type (bits 0-1), protocol
 version (2-5), discover route (6-7), multicast (8), security (9),
 source route (10), destination IEEE (11), source IEEE (12).

  zb-nwk-type-data : Integer = 0
  zb-nwk-type-command : Integer = 1
  zb-nwk-version : Integer = 2

  zb-nwk-fc : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  zb-nwk-fc (ftype) (version) (discover) (security) =
   bit-or (bit-or ftype (bit-shl version 2)) (bit-or (bit-shl discover 6) (bit-shl security 9))

Section: APS Frame Control

 The APS frame control (one byte): frame type (bits 0-1), delivery mode
 (2-3), ack format (4), security (5), ack request (6), extended header
 (7). Delivery mode 0 is unicast.

  zb-aps-type-data : Integer = 0
  zb-aps-type-command : Integer = 1

  zb-aps-fc : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  zb-aps-fc (ftype) (delivery) (ackreq) (security) =
   bit-or (bit-or ftype (bit-shl delivery 2)) (bit-or (bit-shl security 5) (bit-shl ackreq 6))

Section: Helpers

  zb-u16-le : Integer -> List Integer
  zb-u16-le (v) = [bit-and v 255, bit-and (bit-shru v 8) 255]

Section: NWK Frame

  zb-build-nwk-data : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zb-build-nwk-data (dest) (src) (radius) (seq) (payload) =
   zb-u16-le (zb-nwk-fc zb-nwk-type-data zb-nwk-version 0 0) & zb-u16-le dest & zb-u16-le src & [radius, seq] & payload

Section: APS Frame

  zb-build-aps-data : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  zb-build-aps-data (dest-ep) (cluster) (profile) (src-ep) (counter) (payload) =
   [zb-aps-fc zb-aps-type-data 0 0 0, dest-ep] & zb-u16-le cluster & zb-u16-le profile & [src-ep, counter] & payload
